        .bot-message {
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            padding: 10px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: flex-start;
        }
        .message-content {
            margin-left: 10px;
        }
        .close {
            color: #aaa;
            float: right;
            font-size: 28px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .close:hover,
        .close:focus {
            color: black;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <button id="openModal">Open Chat History</button>

    <div id="myModal" class="modal">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <span class="close" id="closeModal">&times;</span>
            <div class="chat-history">
                <div class="message human-message">
                    <div class="message-content">Hello, how can I help you today?</div>
                </div>
                <div class="message bot-message">
                    <div class="message-content">Hi there! I'm here to assist you. What can I do for you?</div>
                </div>
                <div class="message human-message">
                    <div class="message-content">Can you tell me about your services?</div>
                </div>
                <div class="message bot-message">
                    <div class="message-content">Sure! We offer a variety of services including customer support, technical assistance, and more. How can I help you today?</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Get the modal
        var modal = document.getElementById("myModal");

        // Get the button that opens the modal
        var btn = document.getElementById("openModal");

        // Get the <span> element that closes the modal
        var span = document.getElementById("closeModal");

        // When the user clicks the button, open the modal
        btn.onclick = function() {
            modal.style.display = "block";
        }

        // When the user clicks on <span> (x), close the modal
        span.onclick = function() {
            modal.style.display = "none";
        }

        // When the user clicks anywhere outside of the modal, close it
        window.onclick = function(event) {
            if (event.target == modal) {
                modal.style.display = "none";
            }
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**:
   - A button to open the modal.
   - A modal with a chat history section.
   - Messages are styled to differentiate between human and bot messages.

2. **CSS**:
   - Styles for the modal, chat history, and message content.
   - Flexbox is used to align messages properly.

3. **JavaScript**:
   - Opens and closes the modal when the button or close button is clicked.
   - Closes the modal when clicking outside the modal.

This code will create a simple modal that displays a chat history with 4 messages: 2 from the human and 2 from the bot.

